# MadGraph5 batch script: e+ e- > t t~ NP<=1
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_massless.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The capstone: every real Wilson coefficient on at once, under the model's own
#   restrict_massless.dat -- Z-coupling shifts, top dipoles, scalar/vector/tensor
#   four-fermion contact terms and the {mW, mZ, GF} input shifts all contributing
#   to one process. sqrt(s) = 500 GeV clears 2*MT.
#
#   Note what restrict_massless.dat does not switch on: its SMEFTcpv block is
#   zero throughout, so no CP-odd operator contributes here. The `Epsilon`
#   structures are covered by the gg_to_h_cpodd, ee_to_wpwm_cw and gg_to_gg_cg
#   rows, whose cards choose CP-odd values the shipped card leaves at zero.
#
#   This is the row that owns the fixed-energy cross section.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# Orders are explicit because SMEFTsim gives NP hierarchy 99: MadGraph's default
# WEIGHTED bound would drop every diagram carrying a Wilson coefficient.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-massless
display interactions
generate e+ e- > t t~ NP<=1
output ee_to_ttx_smeft -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
